{"Race condition in concurrent index builds: Moving the mutex lock from the start of BuildIndex to only around the cache write allows multiple goroutines to call BuildIndex for the same key concurrently, causing failures when both threads attempt to call bleve.New() on the same directory path for file-based indexes, and risking event loss when the cache is overwritten by a concurrent build": 0.9096682667732239, "Initialization order change can leak goroutines on failure: The search.init function starts goroutines using context.Background() that run forever, and if search.init succeeds but initWatcher then fails, NewResourceServer returns an error but the goroutines from search.init remain running with no way to stop them": 0.8472962379455566, "Duplicate error logging for initialization failure: When Init() fails, the same error message 'error initializing resource server' is logged twice - once inside Init() and again in NewResourceServer() after Init() returns, creating redundant log entries": 0.8181141018867493}